From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <81541646+RyanTheTide@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 23:12:56 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] tests: Read back gamma ramps applied in the compositor

Add meta-gamma-test-utils: a test pattern (gray, red, green, blue and a
mixed band, one column per 8 bit level), and a check that repaints the
view and compares its onscreen framebuffer with the pattern mapped
through the expected ramp, with the interpolation a KMS gamma LUT uses.

gamma-control: a CRTC with neither gamma LUT nor CTM now gets the ramp
in the compositor (shader); a curved ramp on such a CRTC and on a
CTM-only one reads back exactly, and the default path stays pixel
identical before and after; a curved ramp on a CTM-only CRTC no longer
goes to the CTM (ctm, ctm-night-light), a linear one still does
(ctm-linear); night light without a CTM reads back exactly, yields to a
client ramp and comes back at its new temperature (shader-night-light).

color-management: an ICC profile with a VCGT on a CTM-only CRTC gets the
same ramps a gamma LUT would, with and without night light, and they
read back exactly (calibrated-shader); night light is supported on a
CRTC with neither property.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
